# Line endings for files that Linux/WSL executes or parses.
#
# Git already stores every file listed below with LF — `git ls-files --eol`
# reports i/lf across the board. The bug this file fixes is on CHECKOUT: with
# core.autocrlf=true and no attributes, a fresh clone on Windows writes CRLF
# into the working tree, and bash then refuses to run the scripts:
#
#   render_inbound_dialplan.sh: line 26: $'\r': command not found
#   render_inbound_dialplan.sh: line 27: set: pipefail: invalid option name
#
# That is not hypothetical. tests/test_freeswitch_dialplan_template.py passes
# in a long-lived working tree whose copy predates the conversion, and fails in
# a clean worktree of the same commit.
#
# Deliberately scoped: no blanket `* text=auto`. Only files that are executed
# or read on Linux are pinned, so unrelated files keep their current handling
# and no mass renormalization is triggered.

# Shell scripts — run by bash in WSL, in the backend container, and on the
# deployment host. A single CR makes them unrunnable.
*.sh                            text eol=lf

# Container build and runtime inputs.
Dockerfile                      text eol=lf
.dockerignore                   text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml              text eol=lf

# nginx configs, parsed inside Linux containers.
# Currently frontend/nginx.conf and nginx/conf.d/organizer.conf.
*.conf                          text eol=lf

# Env templates. These get copied to .env and read by `docker --env-file`,
# which keeps a trailing CR as part of the value rather than stripping it.
# Matches .env.example at the repo root, backend/, and frontend/.
.env.example                    text eol=lf

# FreeSWITCH dialplan and gateway XML, read by FreeSWITCH in WSL. Scoped to
# this directory on purpose rather than a blanket *.xml, so any Windows-side
# XML added later is unaffected.
backend/voice/freeswitch/*.xml  text eol=lf

# Windows-native tooling keeps CRLF.
*.bat                           text eol=crlf
*.cmd                           text eol=crlf
*.ps1                           text eol=crlf
